course: dictionary
lesson: 15022
title: Respire: breathing and releasing energy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To respire means to breathe, but in science it means something more. Respiration is the process where living things release energy from food, called glucose, inside their cells. It usually uses oxygen and gives out carbon dioxide and water.
explain: Breathing and respiration are not the same. Breathing moves air in and out of your lungs. Respiration happens inside every cell and releases the energy you need to move, grow and keep warm. Your lungs help you breathe, but your cells respire.
explain: All living things respire, not just animals. «Plants respire day and night.» Whether a plant is in sunlight or in the dark, its cells are still releasing energy from food.
fact: To respire means to breathe, and in science it means to release energy from food inside the cells.
fact: Respiration usually uses oxygen and gives out carbon dioxide and water.
fact: Breathing moves air in and out of the lungs. Respiration happens inside cells.
fact: «Plants respire day and night.» Plants and animals both respire.
fact: «Explain how muscles respire.» means describe how muscles release energy from food.
exercise: «Plants respire day and night.» In science, what does respire mean here? | *To release energy from food inside the cells | To sleep in the dark | To make food from sunlight | To move water up the stem
exercise: Which is the best description of breathing? | *Moving air in and out of the lungs | Pumping blood around the body | Making food from sunlight | Releasing energy inside cells
exercise: «Explain how muscles respire.» What is this question asking you to do? | Draw a picture of a lung | Count how many breaths you take in a minute | Name the muscles in your arm | *Describe how muscles release energy from food
test: Respiration usually uses which gas, and gives out carbon dioxide and water? | *Oxygen | Hydrogen | Helium | Nitrogen
test: «All living things respire.» Which of these is living, so it respires? | A cup | A pebble | A rock | *A tree
exam: «Breathing is not the same as respiration.» Which statement is correct? | Breathing and respiration are the same process | *Breathing moves air in and out, while respiration releases energy inside cells | Respiration moves air in and out of the lungs | Breathing releases energy inside cells
